items/thm-p-series-rational.md:51:$1/0^{p}$ is undefined: [[def-rational-power]] gives $0^{p} = 0$ for rational
items/thm-p-series-rational.md:58:powers of a positive base are what [[def-rational-power]] supplies; real exponents
items/thm-p-series-rational.md:67:[L1] Rational powers of a positive base are positive, and $a^{r+s} = a^{r}a^{s}$, $(a^{r})^{s} = a^{rs}$, $a^{-r} = 1/a^{r}$ for $a > 0$ and rationals $r, s$ ([[lem-rational-power-laws]]).
items/thm-p-series-rational.md:71:[L3] The integer power and the rational power agree at an integer exponent: for $a > 0$ and $n \in \mathbb{Z}$, $a^{n}$ read as in [[def-integer-power]] equals $a^{n}$ read as in [[def-rational-power]], since $n = n/1$ and $a^{1/1} = a$ ([[thm-nth-roots-exist]], [[def-rational-power]]). In particular $a^{0} = 1$.
