+{"id":"fs-evt-holds-on-every-bounded-domain","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"af098406d0660cb07c8efe4a231650c089948e94f644fcbab45bf8f431cccc06","outcome":"false_positive","item_sha256":"1829393d8ce64fc2bf811c7477473ce2dc37e06020162bed23b74e24dc673ff7","verdict_item_sha256":"902d0650f650fb477a8f64a1c7b87b14479fe61736592623e22ab6d28541fb81","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-09T08:03:46Z","note":"The cited order fact does supply the alleged missing construction. def-ordered-field states verbatim, 'By trichotomy applied to b-a, for any a,b exactly one of a < b, a = b, a > b holds; this makes <= a total order.' Thus max{1/2,1-epsilon/2} is one of its two displayed members by a two-case comparison. [L4] supplies the ordered-field arithmetic showing that member lies in (0,1) and exceeds 1-epsilon. No new existence principle or dependency is needed, so no edit is permitted."}
+{"id":"thm-continuous-image-of-a-compact-set-r","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"434414bf9332825d9963055bf3753c8e4c264fa2dce4da64b10fc6854b6f2d76","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"a5d7a5f1807ae9e80a7ae3a80a1e03a7dec29925403525323af0e1addf3c9177","verdict_item_sha256":"d46870f38f1423f0ef5473270dc48625a5038f14af0a54310d8b99bada322908","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-09T08:03:46Z","note":"Terra identifies a literal editorial tension, not a mathematical contradiction. The current theorem is a signpost saying the duplication 'is acknowledged in exactly one place' and points to lem-real-and-metric-notions-agree; that lemma says verbatim, 'This item is the single place in the library where that duplication is acknowledged,' meaning the single formal dictionary that reconciles the two vocabularies. The theorem, hypotheses, and proof are unaffected. Treating the signpost itself as a second formal reconciliation is at most a localized wording overstatement, hence nonfatal and uneditable at A8."}
+{"id":"lem-paracompact-hausdorff-cover-shrinking","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"602d1e306532760f54b6c07170bc2f711bc331e54d94a9b7ede3fe9e4cdffadf","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"51ecae7021ef8d83ac64c6fbdb32a145a4124a6b7642e31de5c76a01d07bf0a8","verdict_item_sha256":"55760f96650fadd4302ed753ecf4626d7830798a3509e26d1b46929082c1464b","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-09T08:03:46Z","note":"F1 is locally compressed, because the library's bare definition of refinement does not imply covering. Its cited source def-paracompact-space nevertheless states the exact fact step 1.1 uses: 'every open cover U of X has an open refinement V which covers X and is locally finite,' and repeats this as 'there is a locally finite open cover V'. A competent reader restores the omitted word from the cited definition in seconds. This is nonfatal citation compression, so R1 licenses no edit."}
+{"id":"lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"44169a618efadb4fd877829e8f4e2b8e93fbcd27efdee5b91d663fea265ba306","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"fef19072a284dcbfd3288a8282a7c5043c22a376c20d26dbdb88a098e65d2aaa","verdict_item_sha256":"ad4ee697b22ebdedc41eb9c3f018206e79107236e122642b79e32815c64693dc","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-09T08:03:46Z","note":"Terra correctly observes that L6's cited power definition and geometric-series theorem do not themselves state positivity. The same item's [L9] cites the ordered-field sign rules, and induction from theta^0=1 and theta^(k+1)=theta^k theta proves positivity immediately; lem-power-monotone records the exact conclusion in step 2.1: 'if a > 0 it is a product of two positives, hence > 0.' This standard one-line induction closes well inside thirty seconds and leaves the interval-cover argument intact. R1 licenses no edit."}
+{"id":"cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"6c8c857e5d4fe3bf46e1842f8ff940ad591b548ccef8a5459ae69f598c177a5f","outcome":"confirmed_fatal","defect_type":"other","item_sha256":"0c233b550b97c24e0a2260aee6c6a5567188595839a2ca772764d23f3c2b61f5","verdict_item_sha256":"8dfaf08dc3d49e97498b13ecc81fda7bcf6c3037967d65b8e058c906aa066629","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-09T08:03:46Z","note":"Confirmed as a false reader-visible Facts assertion, not a proof-step gap. L1 says verbatim, 'an at most countable family may be presented as a sequence indexed by N'; for the empty family no function N -> emptyset exists. def-countable only says, 'A is at most countable if it is finite or countably infinite,' and its own Remark directs the nonempty enumeration equivalence to lem-countable-iff-surjection-from-n. The binding thirty-second rule applies to logical gaps, not false general assertions. The clause is unused: step 1.2 instead invokes the preceding exact fact Q approximately N to choose beta:N -> Q. The minimal licensed repair is therefore to delete only the false clause and its now-unused direct dependency/citation, leaving every theorem claim and proof step unchanged."}
