+{"id":"fs-evt-holds-on-every-bounded-domain","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"af098406d0660cb07c8efe4a231650c089948e94f644fcbab45bf8f431cccc06","outcome":"false_positive","item_sha256":"1829393d8ce64fc2bf811c7477473ce2dc37e06020162bed23b74e24dc673ff7","verdict_item_sha256":"902d0650f650fb477a8f64a1c7b87b14479fe61736592623e22ab6d28541fb81","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-09T08:03:46Z","note":"The cited order fact does supply the alleged missing construction. def-ordered-field states verbatim, 'By trichotomy applied to b-a, for any a,b exactly one of a < b, a = b, a > b holds; this makes <= a total order.' Thus max{1/2,1-epsilon/2} is one of its two displayed members by a two-case comparison. [L4] supplies the ordered-field arithmetic showing that member lies in (0,1) and exceeds 1-epsilon. No new existence principle or dependency is needed, so no edit is permitted."}
