+{"id":"thm-infinite-product-criterion","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"758abfc228969b2ea954c97072d36b8a4bcdb9246edc7093b23db9dd11cdde43","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"f06362e6e85a0cdd12ea0ddd951f8eba54914d0c9f43dac3e96d0a669a34f27e","verdict_item_sha256":"76262862432c1d9757e46e87a23864cf2b5771e7ccf54cbf56d6970825b5e583","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-09T08:03:46Z","note":"Terra correctly identifies a local citation omission: lem-of-abs-value states verbatim '$|x| \\ge 0; \\quad |x| = 0 \\iff x = 0; \\quad -|x| \\le x \\le |x|; \\quad |-x| = |x|; \\quad |xy| = |x|\\,|y|$' and does not state the triangle inequality. But lem-of-triangle-inequality states verbatim '$|x + y| \\le |x| + |y|$'; substituting that standard inequality in steps 1.4 and 4.3 closes the citation gap immediately and changes no inference. This is a minor citation quirk below the binding thirty-second threshold, so R1 licenses no edit."}
